      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252895/assets/a32739957ef5ff1bf81f49b1b1baaaab69c6ef3d2613f8ac09ad4020c91c50f7.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the curve shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nHere, the graph is moved left by $4$ units and down by $1$ unit. This corresponds to $h=-4$ and $k=-1.$ So, the equation of the graph is $y=|x+4|-1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252895/assets/fcaf6e4e5e5fa63724be00a344c725e8bc9095c74c8b1114a0dbe90e9ac31935.png)",
